{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PxRyqH4LHJEF2tz4FwbCDL","type":"tool_result","content":"# Goal\n\n**研究任务：模型规模如何影响小型算法任务上的\"延迟泛化\"**\n**背景**\n在模运算等小型算法任务上，神经网络常出现\"延迟泛化\"（grokking）：训练集准确率\n很早就接近 100%，而验证集准确率要在训练很久之后才突然上升。已有工作从电路效率、\n从懒惰状态到丰富状态的训练动力学转变、权重范数等角度解释这一现象。\n\n在模运算类算法任务上，模型规模在延迟泛化中起什么作用，目前缺少系统的实证刻画。\n\n**研究问题**\n请你自主提出并检验一个关于下述问题的可证伪的解释，并用实验支持或反驳它：\n\n> 在模运算类算法任务上，延迟泛化的出现与模型规模之间有什么关系？\n\n**动机**\n厘清模型规模对延迟泛化的作用，可以为选择实验设置提供依据，也能约束对这一现象的各种解释。\n\n**成功如何衡量**\n一个好的回答应当：明确给出你的解释和它的可证伪预测；用本任务内自己运行的实验检验这些预测；\n说明结论的适用范围与不成立的情形。结论可以是支持、反驳或视条件而定。\n\n**关键约束**\n资源与时间预算见 `resources.md`（一周、以 CPU 为主）；数据为程序合成，见 `data.md`；\n最终产出为一篇论文及全部代码，见 `deliverable.md`。\n\n**要求**\n- 研究设计、实验、分析和结论由你自行决定；任务不规定方法或预期结果。\n- 结论必须有实验证据，并说明统计不确定性。\n- 其余约束见同目录的 `starter_literature.md`、`data.md`、`resources.md`、`deliverable.md`。\n\n**起步文献（均发表于 2025-12-16 之前）**\n1. Power, Burda, Edwards, Babuschkin, Misra. *Grokking: Generalization Beyond Overfitting on Small Algorithmic Datasets*. 2022.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.02177\n   说明：在小型算法生成的数据集（含模运算）上研究神经网络的泛化，报告训练集拟合之后很久才出现泛化的现象。\n2. Nanda, Chan, Lieberum, Smith, Steinhardt. *Progress Measures for Grokking via Mechanistic Interpretability*. ICLR 2023.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.05217\n   说明：对在模加法任务上训练的小型 Transformer 做机理可解释性分析，并据此定义训练过程中的进展度量。\n3. Liu, Michaud, Tegmark. *Omnigrok: Grokking Beyond Algorithmic Data*. ICLR 2023.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.01117\n   说明：通过分析损失地形与权重范数来研究延迟泛化，并在图像、语言、分子等任务上进行实验。\n4. Varma, Shah, Kenton, Kramár, Kumar. *Explaining Grokking Through Circuit Efficiency*. 2023.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.02390\n   说明：从电路效率的角度提出对延迟泛化的一种解释，并用训练实验检验由此得出的若干预测。\n5. Kumar, Bordelon, Gershman, Pehlevan. *Grokking as the Transition from Lazy to Rich Training Dynamics*. ICLR 2024.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.06110\n   说明：把延迟泛化与训练动力学从懒惰状态到丰富状态的转变联系起来，并在两层网络的回归设置中分析。\n6. Davies, Langosco, Krueger. *Unifying Grokking and Double Descent*. 2023.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.06173\n   说明：把延迟泛化与双下降两类训练现象放在同一个框架下讨论。\n7. Morris, Sitawarin, Guo, Kokhlikyan, Suh, Rush, Chaudhuri, Mahloujifar. *How much do language models memorize?* 2025.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.24832\n   说明：提出一种估计模型对数据点所含信息量的方法，并在语言模型上进行测量。\n8. Tirumala, Markosyan, Zettlemoyer, Aghajanyan. *Memorization Without Overfitting: Analyzing the Training Dynamics of Large Language Models*. NeurIPS 2022.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.10770\n   说明：在语言模型上实证研究训练过程中对训练数据的记忆。\n9. Zhang, Bengio, Hardt, Recht, Vinyals. *Understanding Deep Learning Requires Rethinking Generalization*. ICLR 2017.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.03530\n   说明：在图像分类网络上研究训练数据的拟合与泛化之间的关系，并检验显式正则化的作用。\n10. Nakkiran, Kaplun, Bansal, Yang, Barak, Sutskever. *Deep Double Descent: Where Bigger Models and More Data Hurt*. ICLR 2020.\n    https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.02292\n    说明：报告多种深度学习任务中，测试表现随模型规模和训练轮数出现的双下降现象。\n11. Loshchilov, Hutter. *Decoupled Weight Decay Regularization*. 2017.\n    https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.05101\n    说明：提出把权重衰减与梯度更新解耦的优化方法 AdamW。\n\n**数据**\n- 主数据：程序合成的算法任务数据，由素数 p 上的模二元运算（例如模加法）生成；对给定 p，\n  输入 (a, b) 共 p² 个，可全部穷举，标签由运算直接计算。格式为整数对到整数的映射，\n  内存中生成即可，体积可忽略。\n- 获取方式：无需下载与账号；不涉及第三方数据，没有许可证问题；没有版本或快照需要固定。\n- 可选：研究需要的其他合成数据可自行生成，并在论文中说明构造方式。\n- 该类数据集的原始定义见 `starter_literature.md` 第 1 条。\n\n**资源与预算**\n- 计算：优先仅使用 CPU；如有需要可使用一张 GPU（单卡即可，不要求特定型号）。\n  具体核数、内存、磁盘以运行环境为准。\n- 时间上限：一周（含实验、写作与整理代码）。\n- 估算依据：任务为小型模型（参数量不超过 10^6 量级）、小数据（输入对数量在 10^4 量级）的训练，\n  单次运行在 CPU 上为分钟至小时级；全部实验合计约数十 CPU 小时。以上为粗略估算，未实测。\n- 存储：需求小（远小于 1 GB）。\n- 不需要大规模集群或付费 API。\n\n**产出要求**\n**提交物**\n1. 一篇完整的研究论文（PDF 与 LaTeX 源文件）。从 ICML、ICLR、NeurIPS 中自选一个会议，使用该会议\n   最新一届的官方 LaTeX 模板，遵守其正文页数上限（参考文献、附录是否计入页数按该会议的规定）；\n   该会议要求随文提交的 checklist（例如 NeurIPS 的 paper checklist）一并填写。论文至少包含摘要、\n   引言、相关工作、方法、实验、讨论与局限、参考文献。\n2. 全部代码与复现说明：环境与依赖版本、数据获取步骤和所用数据的版本、随机种子、运行命令和预计\n   耗时，以及论文中每张表、每张图由哪个脚本生成。\n\n**评审标准**\n论文按所选会议主会的审稿标准评审，重点看：\n\n- 新颖性与定位：贡献是什么，与已有工作的关系和区别是否讲清楚；\n- 严谨性：方法和实验设计是否合理，基线、对照和消融是否恰当，是否报告不确定性（多次运行、\n  置信区间或显著性检验）；\n- 证据是否充分：实验能否支撑论文的每个结论，结论的适用范围是否写清楚；\n- 表达：论文是否清楚、完整，他人能否据此复现；\n- 局限：是否如实讨论方法和结论的局限与失效情形。\n\n负面结果、与预期不符的结果同样有价值；结论有充分证据、不确定性报告完整，比结论本身是正面还是\n负面更重要。\n\n**如实报告（禁止编造）**\n- 论文中的每个数字、每张表和每张图都必须来自你在本任务中实际运行、随附代码可以重新产生的结果；\n  不得编造数据或结果，不得用占位数字、估计值或\"示意\"性的合成结果冒充实测结果。\n- 失败的运行、与预期不符的结果和放弃的方案如实报告；因预算没有完成的实验写明未完成，不写成\n  已完成。\n- 只引用真实存在、你确实查阅过的文献，不得编造引用。\n\n**不得访问的内容**\n本任务的研究问题已有一篇已发表的论文研究过。为保证研究独立，不得检索、访问、阅读或使用：\n\n- 那篇论文本身，及其任何镜像、预印本、摘要页、会议或评审页面、幻灯片、海报、视频、博客和代码\n  仓库；\n- 引用、讨论或复现那篇论文的任何页面，包括后续论文、综述、论文笔记、论文聚合站点和社交媒体\n  讨论。\n\n也不要尝试推测或检索那篇论文的标题、作者或结果。`starter_literature.md` 中的文献，以及与那篇\n论文无关的其他公开文献、数据和代码，可以正常使用。若在检索中偶然遇到上述内容，立即停止阅读，\n并在复现说明中如实记录遇到了什么、在哪里遇到、读到了多少。\n\n# Rubrics\n\nNo rubric is provided for this task; the requirements stated above apply.\n{\n \"schema_version\": 1,\n \"canonical_task\": {\n  \"path\": \"task.md\",\n  \"sha256\": \"b9fae1bccf871cee0078e18f0d291ca240e008d8de4740387583103ba605f1ca\"\n },\n \"method\": {\n  \"class\": \"Evaluator-driven width-scaling study of delayed generalization (grokking): a candidate-owned small one-layer transformer (<=1e6 parameters, AdamW, full-batch, CPU) is trained on modular addition mod a prime p while the evaluator owns data, splits, hyperparameter requests, checkpoint probing, controls, reference trainer and all metrics.\",\n  \"description\": \"Falsifiable hypothesis (tested setting only: modular addition, fixed train fraction, AdamW weight decay 1.0, full-batch updates, one-layer transformer, evaluator-supplied width list): the evaluator-measured grokking delay gap (steps between the first checkpoint with >=99% train accuracy and the first with >=99% validation accuracy, floored at one probe interval, right-censored at the step limit) decreases with model width. Prediction: the cluster-bootstrap (over seeds, 2000 resamples, fixed seed) 95% CI of the OLS slope of ln(delay gap) versus log2(width) lies entirely below zero; refuted if the CI lies at or above zero; inconclusive if it straddles zero or evidence is incomplete. Censored or failed episodes keep the predeclared worst-case delay (the step limit) and are never omitted or renormalized. The claim is cross-checked against an evaluator-owned reference trainer slope and makes no statement about other operations, primes, optimizers, depths or larger models. Candidate-reported state is untrusted; all accuracies, delays, controls and statistics are computed by the evaluator from returned predictions.\"\n },\n \"candidate\": {\n  \"interface\": \"python_rpc_v1:handle\",\n  \"editable_paths\": [\n   \"program_0/src\"\n  ]\n },\n \"evaluators\": {\n  \"search\": \"evaluate.py\",\n  \"final\": \"evaluate_final.py\"\n },\n \"resources\": {\n  \"search_root\": \"resources/search\",\n  \"final_root\": \"resources/final\",\n  \"public_artifact_bundle\": null\n },\n \"data\": {\n  \"search_roles\": [\n   \"search_modular_addition_manifest\"\n  ],\n  \"final_roles\": [\n   \"final_modular_addition_manifest\"\n  ]\n },\n \"metrics\": {\n  \"search\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_modular_addition_manifest\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"final_val_acc_mean\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_modular_addition_manifest\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"censored_fraction\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_modular_addition_manifest\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"control_max_val_acc\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_modular_addition_manifest\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"missing_episodes\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_modular_addition_manifest\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"final\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_modular_addition_manifest\"\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/correct.json\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/evaluation_evidence.json\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/evaluation_manifest.json\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/harness_evaluate_stderr.log\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/harness_evaluate_stdout.log\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/metrics.json\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/program_spec.toml\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/rubric_status.json\n\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1:\nanalysis\ncorrect.json\nevaluation_evidence.json\nevaluation_manifest.json\nharness_evaluate_stderr.log\nharness_evaluate_stdout.log\nmetrics.json\nprogram_spec.toml\nrubric_status.json\nsrc\n\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/analysis:\nmetric_values.csv\nrun_summary.csv\ntimeseries.csv\n\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/src:\ngrok_sweep.py\nprogram.py\n\ntask/program_0:\nprogram_spec.toml\nsrc\n\ntask/resources:\nfinal\nsearch\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Sealed final evaluator for the width-scaling grokking task (self-contained).\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport base64\nimport collections\nimport hashlib\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport queue\nimport re\nimport resource\nimport selectors\nimport signal\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport threading\nimport time\nimport unicodedata\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nBROKER_PROXY_PATH = \"/broker-code/candidate_proxy.py\"\nWIRE_LIMIT = 64 * 1024 * 1024\nSTARTUP_ALLOWANCE = 120.0\nFINISH_RESERVE = 60.0\nEPISODE_OVERHEAD = 15.0\nSTDERR_REPAIR_MODES = (\"AGENTIC_TASK_QUALIFICATION\", \"AGENTIC_TASK_DRAFT_SMOKE\")\nCANDIDATE_THREADS = \"8\"\nSEC_PER_STEP_ESTIMATE = {16: 0.03, 32: 0.04, 64: 0.06, 128: 0.12, 256: 0.35}\n\nPLANE = \"final\"\nPRIMARY_SEEDS = [201, 202, 203, 204]\nRESET_SEQUENCE = [201, 202, 203, 204] * 5 + [201, 201]\nSMOKE_RESET_SEQUENCE = [201, 201, 201]\nWALL_CLOCK_SECONDS = 43200.0\nMAX_RPC_CALLS = 2200         # 22 episodes x (reset + load_train + 40 x (train + predict)) = 1804, plus headroom\nRESET_TIMEOUT = 300.0\nRPC_TIMEOUT_CAP = 1800.0\nREFERENCE_RESERVE = 9000.0\nFIT_THRESHOLD = 0.99\nCONTROL_VAL_CEILING = 0.10\nMIN_CHANGED_FRACTION = 0.9\nBOOTSTRAP_RESAMPLES = 2000\nBOOTSTRAP_SEED = 20260101\nMETRIC_NAMES = (\"combined_score\", \"grok_delay_log_slope\", \"grok_delay_slope_ci_low\",\n                \"grok_delay_slope_ci_high\", \"reference_delay_log_slope\", \"censored_fraction\",\n                \"control_max_val_acc\", \"missing_episodes\")\n\n\ndef ols_slope(x, y):\n    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n    y = np.asarray(y, dtype=float)\n    xc = x - x.mean()\n    denom = float((xc ** 2).sum())\n    if denom == 0.0:\n        return 0.0\n    return float((xc * (y - y.mean())).sum() / denom)\n\n\ndef run_reference_plan(wl, deadline, clock, failures, record_failure):\n    \"\"\"Final reference: first final seed, every width, same checkpoint plan; worst case is slope 0.0.\"\"\"\n    if failures:\n        return None\n    gaps = []\n    steps = [(k + 1) * wl[\"probe_every\"] for k in range(wl[\"n_checkpoints\"])]\n    for width in wl[\"widths\"]:\n        curves, category = run_reference_width(wl, wl[\"seeds_used\"][0], width, wl[\"n_checkpoints\"],\n                                               wl[\"probe_every\"], deadline, clock)\n        if category is not None:\n            record_failure(category)\n            return None\n        gaps.append(delay_gap(steps, curves[\"train_acc\"], curves[\"val_acc\"], wl[\"max_steps\"],\n                              wl[\"probe_every\"])[2])\n    return {\"gaps\": gaps}\n\n\ndef worst_case_metrics(n_episodes):\n    return {\"combined_score\": 0.0, \"grok_delay_log_slope\": 0.0, \"grok_delay_slope_ci_low\": 0.0,\n            \"grok_delay_slope_ci_high\": 0.0, \"reference_delay_log_slope\": 0.0, \"censored_fraction\": 1.0,\n            \"control_max_val_acc\": 1.0, \"missing_episodes\": n_episodes}\n\n\ndef fatal_result(started, smoke):\n    sequence = SMOKE_RESET_SEQUENCE if smoke else RESET_SEQUENCE\n    elapsed = time.monotonic() - started\n    episodes = [{\"seed\": s, \"kind\": \"primary\"} for s in dict.fromkeys(sequence)]\n    outcomes = [{\"score\": 0.0, \"duration\": elapsed / len(episodes)} for _ in episodes]\n    return {\"metrics\": worst_case_metrics(len(sequence)), \"correct\": False,\n            \"evidence\": seed_evidence(episodes, outcomes, [False] * len(episodes)), \"feasible\": False}\n\n\ndef slope_statistics(wl, episodes, outcomes):\n    widths, seeds = wl[\"widths\"], wl[\"seeds_used\"]\n    log_gap = np.zeros((len(widths), len(seeds)))\n    for i, e in enumerate(episodes):\n        if e[\"kind\"] == \"primary\":\n            log_gap[widths.index(e[\"width\"]), seeds.index(e[\"seed\"])] = math.log(outcomes[i][\"gap\"])\n    x = np.log2(np.asarray(widths, dtype=float))\n    xc = x - x.mean()\n    denom = float((xc ** 2).sum())\n    point = ols_slope(np.repeat(x, len(seeds)), log_gap.ravel())\n    if denom == 0.0:\n        return point, point, point\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(BOOTSTRAP_SEED)\n    draws = rng.integers(0, len(seeds), size=(BOOTSTRAP_RESAMPLES, len(seeds)))\n    # a seed resamples all of its widths together (cluster bootstrap over seeds)\n    means = log_gap[:, draws].mean(axis=2)                       # [width, resample]\n    slopes = (xc[:, None] * means).sum(axis=0) / denom\n    low, high = np.percentile(slopes, [2.5, 97.5])\n    return point, float(low), float(high)\n\n\ndef aggregate_plane(wl, episodes, outcomes, complete, reference, baseline_failures, elapsed, hard_deadline,\n                    total_rpc, rpc_count, reset_log, sequence):\n    prim = [i for i, e in enumerate(episodes) if e[\"kind\"] == \"primary\"]\n    ctrl = [i for i, e in enumerate(episodes) if e[\"kind\"] != \"primary\"]\n    n_p = len(prim)\n    passed = [False] * len(episodes)\n    for i in prim:\n        passed[i] = outcomes[i][\"complete\"]\n    for i in ctrl:\n        passed[i] = control_passes(outcomes[i])\n    point, low, high = slope_statistics(wl, episodes, outcomes)\n    if reference is None:\n        ref_slope = 0.0\n    else:\n        ref_slope = ols_slope(np.log2(np.asarray(wl[\"widths\"], dtype=float)),\n                              [math.log(g) for g in reference[\"gaps\"]])\n    metrics = {\n        \"combined_score\": seed_width_score(episodes, outcomes, wl),\n        \"grok_delay_log_slope\": point,\n        \"grok_delay_slope_ci_low\": low,\n        \"grok_delay_slope_ci_high\": high,\n        \"reference_delay_log_slope\": ref_slope,\n        \"censored_fraction\": weighted_mean([1.0 if outcomes[i][\"censored\"] else 0.0 for i in prim],\n                                           [1.0 / n_p] * n_p),\n        \"control_max_val_acc\": max(outcomes[i][\"max_val\"] for i in ctrl),\n        \"missing_episodes\": sum(1 for o in outcomes if not o[\"complete\"]),\n    }\n    if tuple(metrics) != METRIC_NAMES or not all(math.isfinite(v) for v in metrics.values()):\n        raise ValueError(\"invalid metric record\")\n    within = elapsed <= WALL_CLOCK_SECONDS - STARTUP_ALLOWANCE\n    ok_budget = within and rpc_count <= MAX_RPC_CALLS and reset_log == list(sequence)\n    ok_run = complete and not baseline_failures and reference is not None\n    trained = any(outcomes[i]['complete'] and outcomes[i]['max_train'] >= FIT_THRESHOLD for i in prim)\n    correct = bool(ok_run and ok_budget and all(passed) and trained)\n    return {\"metrics\": metrics, \"correct\": correct, \"evidence\": seed_evidence(episodes, outcomes, passed),\n            \"feasible\": bool(ok_run and ok_budget)}\n\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- helpers\n\nclass InvalidResetResponse(RuntimeError):\n    pass\n\n\ndef require_reset_ack(response):\n    if type(response) is not dict or set(response) != {\"ok\"} or response[\"ok\"] is not True:\n        raise InvalidResetResponse(\"invalid reset response\")\n\n\ndef bounded_failure_name(value, fallback):\n    return value if isinstance(value, str) and re.fullmatch(r\"[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,79}\", value) else fallback\n\n\nclass RequiredBaselineFailure(RuntimeError):\n    def __init__(self, category):\n        self.category = bounded_failure_name(category, \"invalid_baseline_diagnostic\")\n        super().__init__(\"required baseline failed\")\n\n\nclass CandidateProtocolError(RuntimeError):\n    \"\"\"Malformed candidate response (schema, shape, range, size).\"\"\"\n\n\nclass CandidateRpcError(RuntimeError):\n    \"\"\"Candidate crashed or raised while handling a request.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, category):\n        self.category = bounded_failure_name(category, \"candidate_error\")\n        super().__init__(\"candidate rpc failed\")\n\n\nclass FatalOperationalError(RuntimeError):\n    \"\"\"Broker/transport/budget failure that makes the remaining evidence unobtainable.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef describe_episode_failure(error, operation):\n    context = error\n    for _ in range(8):\n        if isinstance(context, InvalidResetResponse):\n            return {\"component\": \"candidate\", \"category\": \"invalid_reset_response\", \"operation\": \"reset\"}\n        if isinstance(context, RequiredBaselineFailure):\n            return {\"component\": \"baseline\", \"category\": context.category, \"operation\": \"baseline_worker\"}\n        if isinstance(context, CandidateProtocolError):\n            return {\"component\": \"candidate\", \"category\": \"malformed_response\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b3d8743-eb54-4312-8de4-ec74f69e2571","uuid":"677a6636-c45f-4470-a3ba-75855849adfc","timestamp":"2026-11-11T14:10:32.474Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Goal\n\n**研究任务：模型规模如何影响小型算法任务上的\"延迟泛化\"**\n**背景**\n在模运算等小型算法任务上，神经网络常出现\"延迟泛化\"（grokking）：训练集准确率\n很早就接近 100%，而验证集准确率要在训练很久之后才突然上升。已有工作从电路效率、\n从懒惰状态到丰富状态的训练动力学转变、权重范数等角度解释这一现象。\n\n在模运算类算法任务上，模型规模在延迟泛化中起什么作用，目前缺少系统的实证刻画。\n\n**研究问题**\n请你自主提出并检验一个关于下述问题的可证伪的解释，并用实验支持或反驳它：\n\n> 在模运算类算法任务上，延迟泛化的出现与模型规模之间有什么关系？\n\n**动机**\n厘清模型规模对延迟泛化的作用，可以为选择实验设置提供依据，也能约束对这一现象的各种解释。\n\n**成功如何衡量**\n一个好的回答应当：明确给出你的解释和它的可证伪预测；用本任务内自己运行的实验检验这些预测；\n说明结论的适用范围与不成立的情形。结论可以是支持、反驳或视条件而定。\n\n**关键约束**\n资源与时间预算见 `resources.md`（一周、以 CPU 为主）；数据为程序合成，见 `data.md`；\n最终产出为一篇论文及全部代码，见 `deliverable.md`。\n\n**要求**\n- 研究设计、实验、分析和结论由你自行决定；任务不规定方法或预期结果。\n- 结论必须有实验证据，并说明统计不确定性。\n- 其余约束见同目录的 `starter_literature.md`、`data.md`、`resources.md`、`deliverable.md`。\n\n**起步文献（均发表于 2025-12-16 之前）**\n1. Power, Burda, Edwards, Babuschkin, Misra. *Grokking: Generalization Beyond Overfitting on Small Algorithmic Datasets*. 2022.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.02177\n   说明：在小型算法生成的数据集（含模运算）上研究神经网络的泛化，报告训练集拟合之后很久才出现泛化的现象。\n2. Nanda, Chan, Lieberum, Smith, Steinhardt. *Progress Measures for Grokking via Mechanistic Interpretability*. ICLR 2023.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.05217\n   说明：对在模加法任务上训练的小型 Transformer 做机理可解释性分析，并据此定义训练过程中的进展度量。\n3. Liu, Michaud, Tegmark. *Omnigrok: Grokking Beyond Algorithmic Data*. ICLR 2023.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.01117\n   说明：通过分析损失地形与权重范数来研究延迟泛化，并在图像、语言、分子等任务上进行实验。\n4. Varma, Shah, Kenton, Kramár, Kumar. *Explaining Grokking Through Circuit Efficiency*. 2023.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.02390\n   说明：从电路效率的角度提出对延迟泛化的一种解释，并用训练实验检验由此得出的若干预测。\n5. Kumar, Bordelon, Gershman, Pehlevan. *Grokking as the Transition from Lazy to Rich Training Dynamics*. ICLR 2024.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.06110\n   说明：把延迟泛化与训练动力学从懒惰状态到丰富状态的转变联系起来，并在两层网络的回归设置中分析。\n6. Davies, Langosco, Krueger. *Unifying Grokking and Double Descent*. 2023.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.06173\n   说明：把延迟泛化与双下降两类训练现象放在同一个框架下讨论。\n7. Morris, Sitawarin, Guo, Kokhlikyan, Suh, Rush, Chaudhuri, Mahloujifar. *How much do language models memorize?* 2025.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.24832\n   说明：提出一种估计模型对数据点所含信息量的方法，并在语言模型上进行测量。\n8. Tirumala, Markosyan, Zettlemoyer, Aghajanyan. *Memorization Without Overfitting: Analyzing the Training Dynamics of Large Language Models*. NeurIPS 2022.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.10770\n   说明：在语言模型上实证研究训练过程中对训练数据的记忆。\n9. Zhang, Bengio, Hardt, Recht, Vinyals. *Understanding Deep Learning Requires Rethinking Generalization*. ICLR 2017.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.03530\n   说明：在图像分类网络上研究训练数据的拟合与泛化之间的关系，并检验显式正则化的作用。\n10. Nakkiran, Kaplun, Bansal, Yang, Barak, Sutskever. *Deep Double Descent: Where Bigger Models and More Data Hurt*. ICLR 2020.\n    https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.02292\n    说明：报告多种深度学习任务中，测试表现随模型规模和训练轮数出现的双下降现象。\n11. Loshchilov, Hutter. *Decoupled Weight Decay Regularization*. 2017.\n    https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.05101\n    说明：提出把权重衰减与梯度更新解耦的优化方法 AdamW。\n\n**数据**\n- 主数据：程序合成的算法任务数据，由素数 p 上的模二元运算（例如模加法）生成；对给定 p，\n  输入 (a, b) 共 p² 个，可全部穷举，标签由运算直接计算。格式为整数对到整数的映射，\n  内存中生成即可，体积可忽略。\n- 获取方式：无需下载与账号；不涉及第三方数据，没有许可证问题；没有版本或快照需要固定。\n- 可选：研究需要的其他合成数据可自行生成，并在论文中说明构造方式。\n- 该类数据集的原始定义见 `starter_literature.md` 第 1 条。\n\n**资源与预算**\n- 计算：优先仅使用 CPU；如有需要可使用一张 GPU（单卡即可，不要求特定型号）。\n  具体核数、内存、磁盘以运行环境为准。\n- 时间上限：一周（含实验、写作与整理代码）。\n- 估算依据：任务为小型模型（参数量不超过 10^6 量级）、小数据（输入对数量在 10^4 量级）的训练，\n  单次运行在 CPU 上为分钟至小时级；全部实验合计约数十 CPU 小时。以上为粗略估算，未实测。\n- 存储：需求小（远小于 1 GB）。\n- 不需要大规模集群或付费 API。\n\n**产出要求**\n**提交物**\n1. 一篇完整的研究论文（PDF 与 LaTeX 源文件）。从 ICML、ICLR、NeurIPS 中自选一个会议，使用该会议\n   最新一届的官方 LaTeX 模板，遵守其正文页数上限（参考文献、附录是否计入页数按该会议的规定）；\n   该会议要求随文提交的 checklist（例如 NeurIPS 的 paper checklist）一并填写。论文至少包含摘要、\n   引言、相关工作、方法、实验、讨论与局限、参考文献。\n2. 全部代码与复现说明：环境与依赖版本、数据获取步骤和所用数据的版本、随机种子、运行命令和预计\n   耗时，以及论文中每张表、每张图由哪个脚本生成。\n\n**评审标准**\n论文按所选会议主会的审稿标准评审，重点看：\n\n- 新颖性与定位：贡献是什么，与已有工作的关系和区别是否讲清楚；\n- 严谨性：方法和实验设计是否合理，基线、对照和消融是否恰当，是否报告不确定性（多次运行、\n  置信区间或显著性检验）；\n- 证据是否充分：实验能否支撑论文的每个结论，结论的适用范围是否写清楚；\n- 表达：论文是否清楚、完整，他人能否据此复现；\n- 局限：是否如实讨论方法和结论的局限与失效情形。\n\n负面结果、与预期不符的结果同样有价值；结论有充分证据、不确定性报告完整，比结论本身是正面还是\n负面更重要。\n\n**如实报告（禁止编造）**\n- 论文中的每个数字、每张表和每张图都必须来自你在本任务中实际运行、随附代码可以重新产生的结果；\n  不得编造数据或结果，不得用占位数字、估计值或\"示意\"性的合成结果冒充实测结果。\n- 失败的运行、与预期不符的结果和放弃的方案如实报告；因预算没有完成的实验写明未完成，不写成\n  已完成。\n- 只引用真实存在、你确实查阅过的文献，不得编造引用。\n\n**不得访问的内容**\n本任务的研究问题已有一篇已发表的论文研究过。为保证研究独立，不得检索、访问、阅读或使用：\n\n- 那篇论文本身，及其任何镜像、预印本、摘要页、会议或评审页面、幻灯片、海报、视频、博客和代码\n  仓库；\n- 引用、讨论或复现那篇论文的任何页面，包括后续论文、综述、论文笔记、论文聚合站点和社交媒体\n  讨论。\n\n也不要尝试推测或检索那篇论文的标题、作者或结果。`starter_literature.md` 中的文献，以及与那篇\n论文无关的其他公开文献、数据和代码，可以正常使用。若在检索中偶然遇到上述内容，立即停止阅读，\n并在复现说明中如实记录遇到了什么、在哪里遇到、读到了多少。\n\n# Rubrics\n\nNo rubric is provided for this task; the requirements stated above apply.\n{\n \"schema_version\": 1,\n \"canonical_task\": {\n  \"path\": \"task.md\",\n  \"sha256\": \"b9fae1bccf871cee0078e18f0d291ca240e008d8de4740387583103ba605f1ca\"\n },\n \"method\": {\n  \"class\": \"Evaluator-driven width-scaling study of delayed generalization (grokking): a candidate-owned small one-layer transformer (<=1e6 parameters, AdamW, full-batch, CPU) is trained on modular addition mod a prime p while the evaluator owns data, splits, hyperparameter requests, checkpoint probing, controls, reference trainer and all metrics.\",\n  \"description\": \"Falsifiable hypothesis (tested setting only: modular addition, fixed train fraction, AdamW weight decay 1.0, full-batch updates, one-layer transformer, evaluator-supplied width list): the evaluator-measured grokking delay gap (steps between the first checkpoint with >=99% train accuracy and the first with >=99% validation accuracy, floored at one probe interval, right-censored at the step limit) decreases with model width. Prediction: the cluster-bootstrap (over seeds, 2000 resamples, fixed seed) 95% CI of the OLS slope of ln(delay gap) versus log2(width) lies entirely below zero; refuted if the CI lies at or above zero; inconclusive if it straddles zero or evidence is incomplete. Censored or failed episodes keep the predeclared worst-case delay (the step limit) and are never omitted or renormalized. The claim is cross-checked against an evaluator-owned reference trainer slope and makes no statement about other operations, primes, optimizers, depths or larger models. Candidate-reported state is untrusted; all accuracies, delays, controls and statistics are computed by the evaluator from returned predictions.\"\n },\n \"candidate\": {\n  \"interface\": \"python_rpc_v1:handle\",\n  \"editable_paths\": [\n   \"program_0/src\"\n  ]\n },\n \"evaluators\": {\n  \"search\": \"evaluate.py\",\n  \"final\": \"evaluate_final.py\"\n },\n \"resources\": {\n  \"search_root\": \"resources/search\",\n  \"final_root\": \"resources/final\",\n  \"public_artifact_bundle\": null\n },\n \"data\": {\n  \"search_roles\": [\n   \"search_modular_addition_manifest\"\n  ],\n  \"final_roles\": [\n   \"final_modular_addition_manifest\"\n  ]\n },\n \"metrics\": {\n  \"search\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_modular_addition_manifest\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"final_val_acc_mean\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_modular_addition_manifest\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"censored_fraction\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_modular_addition_manifest\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"control_max_val_acc\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_modular_addition_manifest\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"missing_episodes\",\n    \"data_role\": \"search_modular_addition_manifest\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"final\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n    \"data_role\": \"final_modular_addition_manifest\"\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/correct.json\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/evaluation_evidence.json\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/evaluation_manifest.json\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/harness_evaluate_stderr.log\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/harness_evaluate_stdout.log\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/metrics.json\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/program_spec.toml\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/rubric_status.json\n\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1:\nanalysis\ncorrect.json\nevaluation_evidence.json\nevaluation_manifest.json\nharness_evaluate_stderr.log\nharness_evaluate_stdout.log\nmetrics.json\nprogram_spec.toml\nrubric_status.json\nsrc\n\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/analysis:\nmetric_values.csv\nrun_summary.csv\ntimeseries.csv\n\nresults/ideas/03_effective_learning_rate_confound_width_scaled_hidden_layer_reparametrization_and_grokking_delay/program_1/src:\ngrok_sweep.py\nprogram.py\n\ntask/program_0:\nprogram_spec.toml\nsrc\n\ntask/resources:\nfinal\nsearch\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Sealed final evaluator for the width-scaling grokking task (self-contained).\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport base64\nimport collections\nimport hashlib\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport queue\nimport re\nimport resource\nimport selectors\nimport signal\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport threading\nimport time\nimport unicodedata\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nBROKER_PROXY_PATH = \"/broker-code/candidate_proxy.py\"\nWIRE_LIMIT = 64 * 1024 * 1024\nSTARTUP_ALLOWANCE = 120.0\nFINISH_RESERVE = 60.0\nEPISODE_OVERHEAD = 15.0\nSTDERR_REPAIR_MODES = (\"AGENTIC_TASK_QUALIFICATION\", \"AGENTIC_TASK_DRAFT_SMOKE\")\nCANDIDATE_THREADS = \"8\"\nSEC_PER_STEP_ESTIMATE = {16: 0.03, 32: 0.04, 64: 0.06, 128: 0.12, 256: 0.35}\n\nPLANE = \"final\"\nPRIMARY_SEEDS = [201, 202, 203, 204]\nRESET_SEQUENCE = [201, 202, 203, 204] * 5 + [201, 201]\nSMOKE_RESET_SEQUENCE = [201, 201, 201]\nWALL_CLOCK_SECONDS = 43200.0\nMAX_RPC_CALLS = 2200         # 22 episodes x (reset + load_train + 40 x (train + predict)) = 1804, plus headroom\nRESET_TIMEOUT = 300.0\nRPC_TIMEOUT_CAP = 1800.0\nREFERENCE_RESERVE = 9000.0\nFIT_THRESHOLD = 0.99\nCONTROL_VAL_CEILING = 0.10\nMIN_CHANGED_FRACTION = 0.9\nBOOTSTRAP_RESAMPLES = 2000\nBOOTSTRAP_SEED = 20260101\nMETRIC_NAMES = (\"combined_score\", \"grok_delay_log_slope\", \"grok_delay_slope_ci_low\",\n                \"grok_delay_slope_ci_high\", \"reference_delay_log_slope\", \"censored_fraction\",\n                \"control_max_val_acc\", \"missing_episodes\")\n\n\ndef ols_slope(x, y):\n    x = np.asarray(x, dtype=float)\n    y = np.asarray(y, dtype=float)\n    xc = x - x.mean()\n    denom = float((xc ** 2).sum())\n    if denom == 0.0:\n        return 0.0\n    return float((xc * (y - y.mean())).sum() / denom)\n\n\ndef run_reference_plan(wl, deadline, clock, failures, record_failure):\n    \"\"\"Final reference: first final seed, every width, same checkpoint plan; worst case is slope 0.0.\"\"\"\n    if failures:\n        return None\n    gaps = []\n    steps = [(k + 1) * wl[\"probe_every\"] for k in range(wl[\"n_checkpoints\"])]\n    for width in wl[\"widths\"]:\n        curves, category = run_reference_width(wl, wl[\"seeds_used\"][0], width, wl[\"n_checkpoints\"],\n                                               wl[\"probe_every\"], deadline, clock)\n        if category is not None:\n            record_failure(category)\n            return None\n        gaps.append(delay_gap(steps, curves[\"train_acc\"], curves[\"val_acc\"], wl[\"max_steps\"],\n                              wl[\"probe_every\"])[2])\n    return {\"gaps\": gaps}\n\n\ndef worst_case_metrics(n_episodes):\n    return {\"combined_score\": 0.0, \"grok_delay_log_slope\": 0.0, \"grok_delay_slope_ci_low\": 0.0,\n            \"grok_delay_slope_ci_high\": 0.0, \"reference_delay_log_slope\": 0.0, \"censored_fraction\": 1.0,\n            \"control_max_val_acc\": 1.0, \"missing_episodes\": n_episodes}\n\n\ndef fatal_result(started, smoke):\n    sequence = SMOKE_RESET_SEQUENCE if smoke else RESET_SEQUENCE\n    elapsed = time.monotonic() - started\n    episodes = [{\"seed\": s, \"kind\": \"primary\"} for s in dict.fromkeys(sequence)]\n    outcomes = [{\"score\": 0.0, \"duration\": elapsed / len(episodes)} for _ in episodes]\n    return {\"metrics\": worst_case_metrics(len(sequence)), \"correct\": False,\n            \"evidence\": seed_evidence(episodes, outcomes, [False] * len(episodes)), \"feasible\": False}\n\n\ndef slope_statistics(wl, episodes, outcomes):\n    widths, seeds = wl[\"widths\"], wl[\"seeds_used\"]\n    log_gap = np.zeros((len(widths), len(seeds)))\n    for i, e in enumerate(episodes):\n        if e[\"kind\"] == \"primary\":\n            log_gap[widths.index(e[\"width\"]), seeds.index(e[\"seed\"])] = math.log(outcomes[i][\"gap\"])\n    x = np.log2(np.asarray(widths, dtype=float))\n    xc = x - x.mean()\n    denom = float((xc ** 2).sum())\n    point = ols_slope(np.repeat(x, len(seeds)), log_gap.ravel())\n    if denom == 0.0:\n        return point, point, point\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(BOOTSTRAP_SEED)\n    draws = rng.integers(0, len(seeds), size=(BOOTSTRAP_RESAMPLES, len(seeds)))\n    # a seed resamples all of its widths together (cluster bootstrap over seeds)\n    means = log_gap[:, draws].mean(axis=2)                       # [width, resample]\n    slopes = (xc[:, None] * means).sum(axis=0) / denom\n    low, high = np.percentile(slopes, [2.5, 97.5])\n    return point, float(low), float(high)\n\n\ndef aggregate_plane(wl, episodes, outcomes, complete, reference, baseline_failures, elapsed, hard_deadline,\n                    total_rpc, rpc_count, reset_log, sequence):\n    prim = [i for i, e in enumerate(episodes) if e[\"kind\"] == \"primary\"]\n    ctrl = [i for i, e in enumerate(episodes) if e[\"kind\"] != \"primary\"]\n    n_p = len(prim)\n    passed = [False] * len(episodes)\n    for i in prim:\n        passed[i] = outcomes[i][\"complete\"]\n    for i in ctrl:\n        passed[i] = control_passes(outcomes[i])\n    point, low, high = slope_statistics(wl, episodes, outcomes)\n    if reference is None:\n        ref_slope = 0.0\n    else:\n        ref_slope = ols_slope(np.log2(np.asarray(wl[\"widths\"], dtype=float)),\n                              [math.log(g) for g in reference[\"gaps\"]])\n    metrics = {\n        \"combined_score\": seed_width_score(episodes, outcomes, wl),\n        \"grok_delay_log_slope\": point,\n        \"grok_delay_slope_ci_low\": low,\n        \"grok_delay_slope_ci_high\": high,\n        \"reference_delay_log_slope\": ref_slope,\n        \"censored_fraction\": weighted_mean([1.0 if outcomes[i][\"censored\"] else 0.0 for i in prim],\n                                           [1.0 / n_p] * n_p),\n        \"control_max_val_acc\": max(outcomes[i][\"max_val\"] for i in ctrl),\n        \"missing_episodes\": sum(1 for o in outcomes if not o[\"complete\"]),\n    }\n    if tuple(metrics) != METRIC_NAMES or not all(math.isfinite(v) for v in metrics.values()):\n        raise ValueError(\"invalid metric record\")\n    within = elapsed <= WALL_CLOCK_SECONDS - STARTUP_ALLOWANCE\n    ok_budget = within and rpc_count <= MAX_RPC_CALLS and reset_log == list(sequence)\n    ok_run = complete and not baseline_failures and reference is not None\n    trained = any(outcomes[i]['complete'] and outcomes[i]['max_train'] >= FIT_THRESHOLD for i in prim)\n    correct = bool(ok_run and ok_budget and all(passed) and trained)\n    return {\"metrics\": metrics, \"correct\": correct, \"evidence\": seed_evidence(episodes, outcomes, passed),\n            \"feasible\": bool(ok_run and ok_budget)}\n\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- helpers\n\nclass InvalidResetResponse(RuntimeError):\n    pass\n\n\ndef require_reset_ack(response):\n    if type(response) is not dict or set(response) != {\"ok\"} or response[\"ok\"] is not True:\n        raise InvalidResetResponse(\"invalid reset response\")\n\n\ndef bounded_failure_name(value, fallback):\n    return value if isinstance(value, str) and re.fullmatch(r\"[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,79}\", value) else fallback\n\n\nclass RequiredBaselineFailure(RuntimeError):\n    def __init__(self, category):\n        self.category = bounded_failure_name(category, \"invalid_baseline_diagnostic\")\n        super().__init__(\"required baseline failed\")\n\n\nclass CandidateProtocolError(RuntimeError):\n    \"\"\"Malformed candidate response (schema, shape, range, size).\"\"\"\n\n\nclass CandidateRpcError(RuntimeError):\n    \"\"\"Candidate crashed or raised while handling a request.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, category):\n        self.category = bounded_failure_name(category, \"candidate_error\")\n        super().__init__(\"candidate rpc failed\")\n\n\nclass FatalOperationalError(RuntimeError):\n    \"\"\"Broker/transport/budget failure that makes the remaining evidence unobtainable.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef describe_episode_failure(error, operation):\n    context = error\n    for _ in range(8):\n        if isinstance(context, InvalidResetResponse):\n            return {\"component\": \"candidate\", \"category\": \"invalid_reset_response\", \"operation\": \"reset\"}\n        if isinstance(context, RequiredBaselineFailure):\n            return {\"component\": \"baseline\", \"category\": context.category, \"operation\": \"baseline_worker\"}\n        if isinstance(context, CandidateProtocolError):\n            return {\"component\": \"candidate\", \"category\": \"malformed_response\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
